01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Tupac: Resurrection is a 2003 American documentary film about
the life and death of rapper Tupac Shakur.

11
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The film, directed by Lauren Lazin and released by
Paramount Pictures, is narrated by Shakur himself.

12
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
Tupac: Resurrection premiered at the 2003 Sundance Film Festival on January 22, 2003, and
was released in the United States by Paramount Pictures on November 14, 2003.

13
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:06,000
As of July 1, 2008, it had earned over $7.8 million, making it the 21st-highest-grossing
documentary film in the United States - (in nominal dollars, from 1982 to the present).

14
01:38:00,000 --> 01:38:06,000
The film was nominated for the Academy Award for Best
Documentary Feature at the 77th Academy Awards.

15
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
The film explores themes of rap music, hip-hop, blunt, woman director.
